From: OpenHarmony Build System <build@openharmony.io>
Date: Thu, 29 May 2026 10:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add HarmonyOS default paths support

Add conditional compilation for HarmonyOS platform, which doesn't have
standard Linux paths like /var/run and /etc. Use user home directory
instead.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [HarmonyOS specific]
Signed-off-by: OpenHarmony Build System <build@openharmony.io>
---
 src/defaults.h | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/defaults.h b/src/defaults.h
index 1234567..abcdefg 100644
--- a/src/defaults.h
+++ b/src/defaults.h
@@ -63,11 +63,23 @@

 /* Absolute path to pidfile */
+#ifdef __HARMONYOS__
+/* HarmonyOS doesn't have /var/run, use user home directory */
+#define PID_FILE "/storage/Users/currentUser/tmp/var/run/dhcp_probe.pid"
+#else
 #define PID_FILE "/var/run/dhcp_probe.pid"
+#endif

 /* Absolute path to config file */
+#ifdef __HARMONYOS__
+/* HarmonyOS doesn't have /etc, use user home directory */
+#define CONFIG_FILE "/storage/Users/currentUser/tmp/etc/dhcp_probe.cf"
+#else
 #define CONFIG_FILE "/etc/dhcp_probe.cf"
+#endif

 /* Absolute path to current working directory */
 #define CWD "/"
--
2.25.1